# Git writes LF into every working tree, whatever `core.autocrlf` is set to
# locally.
#
# The template already declares `end_of_line = lf` in .editorconfig, but that
# binds editors — it has no authority over what git puts on disk. On Windows,
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the default, so without this file a checkout arrives
# CRLF, `biome ci` fails on the invisible line terminators, and CI never sees
# it: GitHub runners are Linux and always check out LF.
#
# `text=auto` leaves genuinely binary files alone; only files git detects as
# text are normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf
